#{[17592186056077 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186056082] [17592186058284 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186058286] [17592186058290 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186058292] [17592186059328 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186059333] [17592186059352 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186059354] [17592186086849 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186086851] [17592186091102 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186091107] [17592186097947 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186097952] [17592186097953 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186097958] [17592186097959 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186097962] [17592186098175 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186098176] [17592186100335 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186100340] [17592186100341 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186100346] [17592186102770 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186102772] [17592186103888 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186103889] [17592186113418 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186113420] [17592186113472 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186113476] [17592186114001 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186114006] [17592186114007 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186114012] [17592186114013 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186114014] [17592186115845 :question/worked-solution "Apply the row operation to the identity matrix to obtain the elementary matrix\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac14&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding operation on $A$ is left multiplication:\n\n$$\nEA=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac14&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}A.\n$$"] [17592186115846 :question/worked-solution "Let $A=\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}$. Then\n\n$$\nEA=\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\7&1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\7a+c&7b+d\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe first row is unchanged, and the second row becomes the second row plus seven times the first row. Therefore the operation is $R_2:=R_2+7R_1$."] [17592186118718 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186118719] [17592186118814 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186118818] [17592186120434 :question/worked-solution "Apply $R_1:=R_1+2R_4$, $R_2:=R_2+R_4$, and $R_3:=R_3-2R_4$. Adding a multiple of one row to another does not change the determinant, so it becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}5&0&1&-4\\\\-7&0&-2&2\\\\-11&0&-5&3\\\\2&1&4&-7\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpanding down column $2$, the only nonzero entry is $a_{42}=1$. Its cofactor sign is $(-1)^{4+2}=1$. Therefore the original determinant equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}5&1&-4\\\\-7&-2&2\\\\-11&-5&3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186120450 :question/worked-solution "The determinant of a product equals the product of the determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(A)&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt3&-4\\\\-1&5\\sqrt3\\end{vmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}7&2\\\\5&3\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=(15-4)(21-10)\\\\&=11\\cdot11\\\\&=121.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186183199 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186183200] [17592186184765 :question/worked-solution "First compute\n\n$$\nB^2=\\begin{bmatrix}-2&1\\\\-6&3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2&1\\\\-6&3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4-6&-2+3\\\\12-18&-6+9\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2&1\\\\-6&3\\end{bmatrix}=B.\n$$\n\nThus $B$ is idempotent, so every positive integer power equals $B$. In particular,\n\n$$\nB^5=\\begin{bmatrix}-2&1\\\\-6&3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"]}
